{"paper": "2024-Tier1-25-Sep-2024-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "870", "added": false}, {"text": "804", "added": false}, {"text": "912", "added": false}, {"text": "930", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "Study the given table answer the question that follows. The following table shows the income of a person (in thousand rupees) per annum over the given years. What is the average income from school as a salary per year earned by the person over the given years?", "options": [{"text": "₹1,64,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,74,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,58,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,48,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Simplify: [25 −48 ÷ 6 + 12 × 2] + 78 − [5 + 3 of (25 − 2 × 10)]", "options": [{"text": "98", "added": false}, {"text": "90", "added": false}, {"text": "99", "added": false}, {"text": "89", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "Consider the following table for total exports of goods of 5 companies over 5 years (in lakhs). If the ratio of exports to the imports of companies S and U in the year 2015 is 3 : 2 and 1 : 2, respectively, then, the total imports (in ₹ lakhs) of companies S and U together in the year 2015 is:", "options": [{"text": "121", "added": false}, {"text": "174", "added": false}, {"text": "187", "added": false}, {"text": "157", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "The ratio of expenditure to savings of a woman is 4 : 1. If her income and expenditure are increased by 20% and 10%, respectively, then find the percentage change in her savings.", "options": [{"text": "40%", "added": false}, {"text": "50%", "added": false}, {"text": "60%", "added": false}, {"text": "30%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "A man loses 28% by selling an article for ₹144. If he sells it for ₹288, what will be his gain/loss percentage?", "options": [{"text": "Gain, 41%", "added": false}, {"text": "Loss, 43%", "added": false}, {"text": "Gain, 44%", "added": false}, {"text": "Loss, 46%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1000", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "Find the diameter (in cm) of a circle whose circumference is equal to the sum of the circumferences of two circles of radii 12 cm and 16 cm.", "options": [{"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "56", "added": false}, {"text": "64", "added": false}, {"text": "28", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "In a quadrilateral ABCD, AB = BC, AD = DC. ∠ ABD = 68°, ∠ ADB = (2y-7)°, ∠ BDC = 33°, ∠ DBC = (3x+2)°. Then the value of 2x+3y is:", "options": [{"text": "108", "added": false}, {"text": "144", "added": false}, {"text": "104", "added": false}, {"text": "118", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "45°", "added": false}, {"text": "60°", "added": false}, {"text": "90°", "added": false}, {"text": "30°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "The relation between K1 and K2 for which the system of linear equations K1x + 3y = 8 and 4x + K2y = 16 represents coincident lines, is:", "options": [{"text": "K2 = 3K1", "added": false}, {"text": "K2 + 3K1 = 0", "added": false}, {"text": "K2 = K1", "added": false}, {"text": "K1 + K2 = 0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Coordinate Geometry", "sub": "slope-and-line", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Two pipes X and Y can fill a tank in 14 hours and 21 hours, respectively. Both pipes are opened simultaneously to fill the tank. In how many hours will the empty tank be filled?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "combined-pipes", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "The two circles intersect at two points P and Q. PR and PS are diameters of the two circles. What is ∠ PQR ?", "options": [{"text": "90°", "added": false}, {"text": "0°", "added": false}, {"text": "45°", "added": false}, {"text": "60°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "Naman borrows a sum of ₹3,48,020 at the rate of 8% per annum simple interest. At the end of the first year, he repays ₹15,090 towards return of principal amount borrowed. If Naman clears all pending dues at the end of the second year, including interest payment that accrued during the first year, how much does he pay (in ₹) at the end of the second year?", "options": [{"text": "3,79,386", "added": false}, {"text": "3,87,406", "added": false}, {"text": "3,88,931", "added": false}, {"text": "3,92,733", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "A policeman noticed a thief at some distance. The policeman started running to catch the thief and the thief also started running at the same time. The speed of both policeman and the thief was 12 km per hour and 10 km per hour, respectively. It took 30 minutes for the policeman to catch the thief. Find the initial distance (in metres) between them.", "options": [{"text": "500", "added": false}, {"text": "600", "added": false}, {"text": "1000", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "relative-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "38", "added": false}, {"text": "28", "added": false}, {"text": "39", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "6 : 5", "added": false}, {"text": "7 : 8", "added": false}, {"text": "5 : 6", "added": false}, {"text": "8 : 7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "If m is even, then (8m – 1) is divisible by:", "options": [{"text": "63", "added": false}, {"text": "42", "added": false}, {"text": "65", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "Find the value of 'k' for which the system of equations 4x+6y=7 and 6x+(k+4)y-21=0 has a unique solution.", "options": [{"text": "k = 5", "added": false}, {"text": "k ≠ 5", "added": false}, {"text": "k = 7", "added": false}, {"text": "k ≠ 7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "During a new-year sale, a shopkeeper offers a discount scheme to his customers, ‘Buy 5 Sweaters, Get 2 Sweaters Free’. Find the effective percentage discount given by the shopkeeper.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "In the 8th class, consisting of 30 students, a Mathematics test was taken. 10 students had an average score of 90. The other students had an average score of 75. What is the average score of the whole class?", "options": [{"text": "78", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}, {"text": "76", "added": false}, {"text": "74", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "Find the value of tan 72° − tan 27° − tan 72° tan 27°.", "options": [{"text": "−1", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "−2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "If A:B = 6 : 8 and B:C = 5 : 11, then A:B:C is:", "options": [{"text": "11:23:14", "added": false}, {"text": "14:31:25", "added": false}, {"text": "15:32:44", "added": false}, {"text": "15:20:44", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}]}